      "writtenOn": "2017-12-19T02:50:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Will the trailing data be part of RO/RW image? If it is and the size(RO/RW +trailing data) is not more than NPCX_PROGRAM_MEMORY_SIZE, using fixed size should be fine here. \nI agree that It will be better if we can use the actual RO/RW image size here. But I am thinking how to get it during compiling time.\nAlternatively, how about replace this filed like the following scripts in flash_ec?  \n# Read the RO image size                                                         \nEC_IMG_SIZE\u003d$(printf \"%08X\" `stat -c \"%s\" build/npcx7_evb/RO/ec.RO.flat`)           \necho $EC_IMG_SIZE                                                                \n# Covert the value of image size to little endian                                \nEC_IMG_SIZE_LE\u003d${EC_IMG_SIZE:6:2}${EC_IMG_SIZE:4:2}${EC_IMG_SIZE:2:2}${EC_IMG_SIZE:0:2}\necho $EC_IMG_SIZE_LE                                                             \n# Replace actual image size with the default code RAM size                       \nxxd -g4 ${MONITOR_RO_HDR} | awk -v s\u003d\"$EC_IMG_SIZE_LE\" \u0027NR\u003d\u003d1 {$3\u003ds}1\u0027 | xxd -r \u003e monitor_tmp.bin",
      "parentUuid": "279b2105_eb812b77",
